# `yo fix` must SAY it could not repair a file rather than printing "nothing to
# fix", which reads as "this file is clean" — the hollow-success shape
# plans/archive/LLM_FRIENDLY_TOOLCHAIN_AND_SYNTAX.md exists to remove.
#
# The fixture is an E0003 (adjacent different operators need parentheses). It
# reaches the typed stash and carries NO repair, because more than one edit
# fixes it — `(1 && 2) && 3` and `1 && (2 && 3)` are both valid groupings, and
# the compiler never guesses between alternatives.
#
# This case used to carry an UNREPAIRABLE-BY-ACCIDENT fixture: an undefined
# name whose unique rename the compiler had computed but `fix` could not see,
# because the def-time trial flattened evaluator diagnostics to text. That is
# fixed, and the rename is now asserted by fix-applies-an-evaluator-rename. So
# this case keeps the truthfulness assertion with a fixture that genuinely has
# no single correct repair, which is the case the message is FOR.
#
# rc is 1: `fix` exits non-zero while any file still does not evaluate.
stdout_keep=^fix:
timeout=180
